WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:04.950
- [Instructor] You or
someone you care about

00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:08.340
may have been recently
diagnosed with breast cancer.

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:10.530
This video will help you understand

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:12.623
some available treatment options.

00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:15.530
Breast cancer is a disease

00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:17.550
where some of the cells in the breast

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:20.033
begin to grow uncontrollably.

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:24.930
Treatments for breast
cancer can include surgery,

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:29.930
radiation therapy,
chemotherapy, hormone therapy,

00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:33.203
targeted therapy and immunotherapy.

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:36.120
There are several types of surgery

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:39.650
depending on the size and
location of the tumor.

00:00:39.650 --> 00:00:41.350
This video does not cover

00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:45.220
all available types of
breast cancer surgery.

00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:48.370
During a lumpectomy, the tumor is removed

00:00:48.370 --> 00:00:51.493
along with some of the
normal tissue around it.

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:55.970
In a total or simple mastectomy,

00:00:55.970 --> 00:00:58.203
the entire breast is removed.

00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:02.520
During a modified radical mastectomy,

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:05.180
the entire breast is removed.

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:07.390
In addition, some of the lymph nodes

00:01:07.390 --> 00:01:09.010
under your arm are removed

00:01:09.010 --> 00:01:11.793
and sometimes other tissues in your chest.

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:16.650
Your doctor may also want to
give you radiation therapy.

00:01:16.650 --> 00:01:20.540
This therapy uses radiation
to kill the cancer cells

00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:22.740
or keep them from growing.

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:25.900
External beam radiation uses a machine

00:01:25.900 --> 00:01:29.983
outside the body that aims
radiation at the cancer.

00:01:31.690 --> 00:01:33.710
Internal radiation therapy,

00:01:33.710 --> 00:01:37.560
also known as brachytherapy,
uses a substance

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:39.340
that gives off radiation

00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:42.400
through different types
of delivery devices.

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:45.240
The substance is put inside your breast

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:47.453
where the cancer has been removed.

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:52.770
Chemotherapy uses certain
drugs to kill cancer.

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:55.210
These drugs may treat cancer cells

00:01:55.210 --> 00:01:57.210
throughout the whole body

00:01:57.210 --> 00:02:01.113
or can be given to treat
cancer cells in one area.

00:02:02.730 --> 00:02:05.900
Another treatment option
is hormone therapy.

00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:10.150
Hormones are substances
found naturally in your body.

00:02:10.150 --> 00:02:13.380
Estrogen is one of these hormones.

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:16.840
Your body uses estrogen
mainly for the growth

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:20.983
and development of your
uterus, breast and ovaries.

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:25.640
However, estrogen can
also promote the growth

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:29.440
of certain hormone receptor
positive cancer cells.

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:31.490
One type of hormone therapy

00:02:31.490 --> 00:02:35.060
blocks estrogen from binding
to breast cancer cells,

00:02:35.060 --> 00:02:38.893
so it cannot cause cancer
cells to grow and divide.

00:02:39.810 --> 00:02:42.980
Targeted therapy is a
treatment option for cancers

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:46.983
that have a specific kind of
marker on the cancer cells.

00:02:48.210 --> 00:02:53.003
One therapy targets cells
with markers called HER2.

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:58.150
HER2 is a naturally occurring
protein on your cells

00:02:58.150 --> 00:03:01.603
that normally promotes
healthy growth in your cells.

00:03:02.690 --> 00:03:06.043
Some cancer cells have
too much of this protein.

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:10.630
This causes the cancer cells

00:03:10.630 --> 00:03:15.320
to grow and spread more
aggressively than normal cells.

00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:19.020
Targeted therapy drugs are
designed to only attach

00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:22.423
to the HER2 proteins on cancer cells.

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:28.623
As a result, the cancer cells
stop growing and may die.

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:34.800
Immuno-oncology also
known as immunotherapy,

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:38.490
helps your immune system fight cancer.

00:03:38.490 --> 00:03:40.620
Cancer can sometimes hide

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:42.863
from the immune cells that attack them.

00:03:43.850 --> 00:03:46.910
For example, both cancer and immune cells

00:03:46.910 --> 00:03:51.230
may have proteins called
checkpoint proteins.

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:55.763
When they attach, attack from
other immune cells is stopped.

00:03:56.670 --> 00:04:00.780
Scientists are looking at one
type of immunotherapy drug

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:02.990
that blocks the checkpoint proteins

00:04:02.990 --> 00:04:04.733
from attaching to each other.

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:08.500
As a result, the immune cell can attack

00:04:08.500 --> 00:04:10.743
and destroy the cancer cell.

00:04:11.880 --> 00:04:13.490
Your doctor may prescribe

00:04:13.490 --> 00:04:16.020
a combination of the
treatments we've discussed

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:19.253
or different treatment options
than those mentioned here.

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:23.270
If you have questions about breast cancer

00:04:23.270 --> 00:04:26.010
or any medications you
have been prescribed,

00:04:26.010 --> 00:04:27.360
talk to your doctor.

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:30.610
It is important to take
your medications as directed

00:04:30.610 --> 00:04:33.303
and report any side effects you have.

